# ===== Secrets / local config =====
.env
# Teacher profiles ship with the CODE in app/bundled_teachers/ (tracked, no
# personal data) so a fresh clone runs out of the box and they stay readable
# even when data/ is bind-mounted over in a container. data/teachers/ below
# holds only runtime state: its keys are student ids, so it must never be
# published (same rule as the student profiles further down).
data/teachers/

# ===== Personal data (never publish) =====
# Student profiles: name, age, interests, progress
data/students/
# Lesson transcripts: every student/teacher turn
data/sessions/
# Full LLM prompt+response logs (student utterances included)
data/prompt_logs/

# ===== Curriculum =====
# data/curriculum/ holds the user's own textbooks (created and maintained in
# the web UI). Only its README is tracked. The bundled sample textbooks that
# ship with the repo live in app/bundled_curriculum/ (tracked).
data/curriculum/*
!data/curriculum/README.md

# ===== Developer-only tools and notes =====
# Tests never enter the repo (2026-09-25 决定): contract tests, dry-run scripts
# and real-MiMo e2e scripts all stay on the maintainer's machine. The same
# goes for the internal dev journal (docs/开发账本.md + docs/archive/), the
# Feishu interaction-tree design doc, and the ZCode workspace config.
tests/
docs/飞书交互树.md
docs/开发账本.md
docs/archive/
.zcodeignore
.zcode/

# ===== Runtime output =====
logs/
*.log
# session_registry 的跨进程互斥锁文件（运行时状态，按 student_id 一把）
data/session_locks/

# ===== Auto-downloaded ffmpeg (see setup/bootstrap.ps1) =====
# Offline fallback when winget is unavailable; ~90 MB, never belongs in git.
tools/

# ===== Python =====
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ===== Editors / OS =====
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.pytest_tmp
# pytest --basetemp scratch — never belongs in git (a round of basetemp junk
# under .tmp/pytest-qr3 once got committed by accident; untracked 2026-10-14)
.tmp/
# ===== Scratch =====
# temp/ holds working material (textbook PDFs/JSON under review) and must never
# be committed.
temp/
